#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""event-ack — manage the four-tier claude-event response surface.

This CLI is the unified entry point for the **new** event-must-act
infrastructure (refined per Andrew 2026-05-21 — see the PR
description for the design notes). It owns three pieces of state:

  - ``pending-actions.json``  — actionable events waiting on a
    response. The companion ``eval-event-must-act`` evaluator reads
    this file; when non-empty AND the missed-tool-call counter has
    reached the threshold, it DENIES Bash tool calls.

  - ``tool-call-counter.json`` — N-tool-call escalation counter.
    Default threshold N=3 (configurable via ``$EVENT_MUST_ACT_N``).
    Incremented by the evaluator on every non-exempt Bash tool call
    that runs while pending actions exist; reset to 0 on any
    ``event-ack`` call (so a SINGLE actionable event doesn't fire
    the gate immediately — the LLM gets N grace tool calls to
    spawn an agent / ack / dismiss).

  - ``ambient-context.json``  — info-only events queued for the
    next UserPromptSubmit context inject. The companion hook
    ``user-prompt-ambient-inject-hook`` drains this file on every
    user prompt and emits the contents as additional context (no
    blocking, no gate).

Subcommands:

  event-ack ingest --source <src> --tag <tag> --message <msg>
                                  Classify the event (via
                                  ``event-classify``) and route to the
                                  correct queue (pending or ambient).
                                  Signal-tagged events are NO-OP
                                  (intentionally excluded).

  event-ack add "<key>" [--source "<src>"]
                                  Manually add an actionable pending
                                  entry. Equivalent to v1's --add.

  event-ack ack "<key>" --action "<text>"
                                  Mark ONE actionable as handled. Removes
                                  from pending-actions, resets the
                                  N-counter to 0. For a queue-orphaned key
                                  whose item is still `running`, this is
                                  REFUSED unless the item has actually been
                                  resolved (done/abandon/resurrect) -- see
                                  --verified-false-positive below.

  event-ack ack "<key>" --action "<text>" --verified-false-positive
                                  Escape hatch for a queue-orphaned key the
                                  caller has independently confirmed is a
                                  LIVE agent (e.g. verified via agent-tail /
                                  agent-msg / a direct SendMessage reply),
                                  not a dead one. Clears the pending event
                                  WITHOUT touching the queue item itself --
                                  does NOT call done/abandon/resurrect, so a
                                  live agent is never stranded by a rotated
                                  q-id. The destructive resolutions stay
                                  available but become a CHOICE, not the
                                  only way to clear a false-positive alert.
                                  A no-op on a non-orphan key (nothing to
                                  bypass). Still requires a substantive
                                  --action (the ack must say what
                                  verification was done).

  event-ack ack-batch             PERMANENTLY DISABLED (Andrew directive,
                                  2026-09-11, #7784/7786/7787): this became
                                  a reflexive per-event bypass instead of a
                                  deliberate escape hatch, so it is now a
                                  hard, unconditional refusal -- exits
                                  nonzero, touches NO state (no pending
                                  removal, no counter reset, no liveness
                                  stamp) regardless of any flags passed.
                                  Kept registered (not removed) purely so
                                  it stays discoverable in --help instead
                                  of erroring as an unknown subcommand.
                                  Redirects the caller to per-key `ack`.

  event-ack list                  Show pending + counter state.

  event-ack clear                 Clear pending (escape hatch). Counter
                                  is also reset.

  event-ack drain-ambient         (Hook-internal) Pop the queued
                                  ambient events and print them as a
                                  user-prompt context block. Used by
                                  user-prompt-ambient-inject-hook.

  event-ack reset-counter         Reset the N-counter to 0 without
                                  changing pending state.

  event-ack --self-test           Run the embedded test suite.

Liveness
--------

``last-ack-timestamp`` (epoch float) is stamped by every successful per-key
``ack``. Its age is the daemon's ONE liveness signal (``[ack] stale_minutes``
in claude-watch's config): ANY per-key ack proves the main loop is alive, so
a loop busy handling real events never needs a synthetic poke. When nothing
has been acked for ``[cadence] keepalive_interval_secs`` the daemon emits a
``keepalive`` event whose only purpose is to give an IDLE loop something to
ack -- ``event-ack ack "<keepalive-key>" --action "..."`` stamps liveness the
same as any other per-key ack. ``ack-batch`` is PERMANENTLY DISABLED and
stamps NOTHING (see the Subcommands list above) -- it is not a liveness path
any more. The pre-2026-08-22 design instead had the loop ``touch`` a separate
host heartbeat FILE; two signals for one fact, and the file could stay fresh
while events went unread.

Signal-distinct guarantee
-------------------------

This CLI NEVER routes signal-tagged events to either pending-actions
or ambient-context. Signal-DM ack-gating stays on the existing
per-thread obligation (``signal-wait-*`` watcher + ``signal-send``
ack-gate). Andrew (sig_ts 2026-05-21): "for now keep signal distinct
even if it fits conceptually. too mission critical to risk on new
shared infra".

State files
-----------

  - $CLAUDE_EVENT_STATE_DIR/pending-actions.json
  - $CLAUDE_EVENT_STATE_DIR/tool-call-counter.json
  - $CLAUDE_EVENT_STATE_DIR/ambient-context.json

Default: ``~/.config/claude-events/``.

Concurrency: every read-modify-write goes through ``flock(2)`` on a
sidecar lockfile (``<state-file>.lock``). The lock is held for the
entire transaction so two parallel ``event-ack`` invocations cannot
race (q-2026-05-21-856d refinement: file locking was missing in v1).

Default-open: missing / corrupt state files are treated as empty
(no pending, counter=0). The evaluator inherits the same posture.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import errno
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
from contextlib import contextmanager
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

# --- Paths / config -------------------------------------------------------

DEFAULT_STATE_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(
    "CLAUDE_EVENT_STATE_DIR",
    os.path.expanduser("~/.config/claude-events"),
))

PENDING_FILE = "pending-actions.json"
COUNTER_FILE = "tool-call-counter.json"
AMBIENT_FILE = "ambient-context.json"
LAST_ACK_FILE = "last-ack-timestamp"

DEFAULT_N = int(os.environ.get("EVENT_MUST_ACT_N", "3"))


# Pure-liveness source_event values: events that classify ACTIONABLE (so they
# land in pending-actions.json and stamp the gate) but whose ONLY demand is that
# the loop ack to prove it is alive -- there is no substantive action to take.
# keepalive is the daemon's idle-poke; heartbeat-tick is its pre-2026-08-22 name
# (see event-classify). A liveness entry's per-key `ack` does not require a
# substantive --action note (see the `ack` dispatch below); ack-batch is
# PERMANENTLY DISABLED (see below) so it no longer clears anything -- every
# entry, liveness or actionable, is now acked individually via `ack`.
LIVENESS_SOURCE_EVENTS = frozenset({
    "claude-watch/keepalive",
    "claude-watch/heartbeat-tick",
})


def _is_liveness_entry(entry: dict) -> bool:
    """True if a pending entry is a pure-liveness (keepalive/heartbeat-tick)
    event -- acked purely to prove the loop is alive, carrying no real action.
    Identified by the entry's ``source_event`` (``<source>/<tag>``) set at
    ingest time. An entry with no ``source_event`` (e.g. a bare ``add``) is
    treated as actionable -- the safe default is to PROTECT it from batch-ack."""
    return (entry.get("source_event") or "") in LIVENESS_SOURCE_EVENTS


def _state_path(state_dir: Path, name: str) -> Path:
    return state_dir / name


def _lock_path(state_file: Path) -> Path:
    return state_file.with_suffix(state_file.suffix + ".lock")


# --- Locked read-modify-write helper --------------------------------------

@contextmanager
def _locked(state_dir: Path, filename: str):
    """Yield (path, current_dict) under an flock on the sidecar lockfile.
    On exit (no exception), atomically write back via temp+rename. On
    exception, the file is left untouched and the lock released."""
    state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    path = _state_path(state_dir, filename)
    lock = _lock_path(path)
    # Open (or create) the lock file. We hold an exclusive lock for the
    # whole transaction.
    fd = os.open(str(lock), os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        # Read current state (default-open on missing/corrupt).
        if path.exists():
            try:
                data = json.loads(path.read_text())
                if not isinstance(data, dict):
                    data = {}
            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError, OSError):
                data = {}
        else:
            data = {}

        # Hand the caller a dict it can mutate. Wrap in a sentinel so we
        # know whether the caller wants us to write back.
        proxy = {"data": data, "write": False}
        yield proxy

        if proxy["write"]:
            tmp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + ".tmp")
            tmp.write_text(json.dumps(proxy["data"], indent=2,
                                       sort_keys=True))
            os.replace(tmp, path)
    finally:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            os.close(fd)
        except OSError:
            pass


def _now() -> str:
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()


def _update_last_ack_timestamp(state_dir: Path) -> None:
    """Update the last-ack timestamp file to now (Unix epoch seconds).

    This file's mtime serves as the liveness signal for the daemon's
    ack-driven heartbeat detection. ANY event-ack (not just heartbeat-tick)
    refreshes liveness, so a busy loop acking many events stays alive even
    if the heartbeat-tick cadence event never delivers.

    Default-open: write failure is silently swallowed (logged to stderr).
    The ack itself already succeeded; losing the timestamp update is
    recoverable -- the daemon will emit a probe heartbeat-tick, and acking
    that will refresh the timestamp.
    """
    try:
        state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        path = state_dir / LAST_ACK_FILE
        # Write the current Unix epoch as a simple float. This is cheaper
        # than JSON and sufficient for the daemon's mtime + content check.
        now_epoch = datetime.now(timezone.utc).timestamp()
        path.write_text(f"{now_epoch}\n")
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"event-ack: warning: could not update last-ack timestamp: {e}",
              file=sys.stderr)


# --- Core operations ------------------------------------------------------

def add_pending(state_dir: Path, key: str, source: str = "",
                reset_counter: bool = True, reason: str = "",
                unclassified: bool = False) -> dict:
    """Add an entry to pending-actions.json. Reset the N-counter so
    a newly-arrived actionable event doesn't immediately tip a gate
    that was about to fire from a previous burst (each actionable
    event gets a fresh N-call grace window).

    ``reason`` / ``unclassified`` carry the classifier's verdict onto the
    stored entry. ``unclassified`` marks an event that matched NO rule AND
    whose producer shipped no ``data.tier`` -- it landed here via the
    fail-loud default. The gate renders that distinctly so a missing
    classification reads as "add a rule / have the producer ship a tier"
    rather than as mysterious gating (botchat #2483)."""
    added = False
    with _locked(state_dir, PENDING_FILE) as p:
        pending = p["data"].setdefault("pending", [])
        if not any(item.get("key") == key for item in pending):
            entry = {"key": key, "added_at": _now()}
            if source:
                entry["source_event"] = source
            if reason:
                entry["reason"] = reason
            if unclassified:
                entry["unclassified"] = True
            pending.append(entry)
            p["write"] = True
            added = True

    if reset_counter:
        # Reset on transition from non-pending -> pending OR on add of a
        # new key; the simpler invariant "any ack-or-add resets" matches
        # operator mental model (each new event gets a fresh grace).
        _set_counter(state_dir, 0)
    return {"added": added, "key": key}


def _find_pending_entry(state_dir: Path, key: str) -> dict | None:
    """Return a copy of the pending entry with ``key``, or None if absent."""
    with _locked(state_dir, PENDING_FILE) as p:
        for it in p["data"].get("pending", []):
            if it.get("key") == key:
                return dict(it)
    return None


def ack_pending(state_dir: Path, key: str, action: str) -> dict:
    """Remove an entry from pending-actions.json. Reset the N-counter.

    Also updates the last-ack timestamp, which serves as the liveness signal
    for the daemon's ack-driven heartbeat detection (any ack refreshes
    liveness, not just heartbeat-tick acks).
    """
    removed = False
    remaining = 0
    with _locked(state_dir, PENDING_FILE) as p:
        pending = p["data"].setdefault("pending", [])
        original = len(pending)
        new_pending = [it for it in pending if it.get("key") != key]
        if len(new_pending) != original:
            removed = True
        p["data"]["pending"] = new_pending
        p["write"] = True
        remaining = len(new_pending)

    # Reset counter on any ack (whether the key was present or not -- the
    # idempotent ack should still relax the gate).
    _set_counter(state_dir, 0)

    # Update liveness timestamp: ANY ack proves the loop is alive.
    _update_last_ack_timestamp(state_dir)

    return {"removed": removed, "key": key, "action": action,
            "remaining": remaining}


# Source-event tags that mark a queue-orphaned actionable event -- the daemon's
# WorkQueueOrphaned / running-without-owner alert. Acking one of these does NOT
# resolve the underlying orphan: a still-``running`` item with no live owner
# stays orphaned. So the ack of such a key is gated on the item no longer being
# ``running`` (resolved via done / abandon / resurrect first).
QUEUE_ORPHANED_SOURCE_EVENTS = (
    "queue/queue-orphaned", "claude-watch/queue-orphaned")

# Queue ids are ``q-YYYY-MM-DD-XXXX`` (XXXX is an alphanumeric suffix).
_QID_RE = re.compile(r"q-\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-[0-9A-Za-z]+")


def _resolve_session_task_cli() -> str | None:
    """Locate the session-task CLI: PATH first, then the sibling source tree
    (``tools/session-task/session-task``) when running from a checkout."""
    cli = shutil.which("session-task")
    if cli:
        return cli
    sibling = (Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
               / "session-task" / "session-task")
    if sibling.exists():
        return str(sibling)
    return None


def verify_orphan_resolved(
    entry: dict | None, key: str, *, verified_false_positive: bool = False,
) -> tuple[bool, str]:
    """Gate the ack of a queue-orphaned event on the orphan being resolved.

    Returns ``(ok, message)``. ``ok=True`` allows the ack; ``ok=False`` refuses
    it, with ``message`` explaining why.

    Only queue-orphaned keys are gated (identified by the entry's
    ``source_event`` being ``queue/queue-orphaned`` or
    ``claude-watch/queue-orphaned``). For those, the q-id is parsed from the key
    (which carries the event message) and looked up via ``session-task queue
    show``. A still-``running`` item is REFUSED -- acking does not resolve an
    orphan; the item must be resolved via done / abandon / resurrect first. Any
    other status (done, abandoned, blocked, pending, not-found, ...) is allowed.

    ``verified_false_positive=True`` (``event-ack ack --verified-false-positive``)
    is the escape hatch for the case the hard refusal otherwise forces into a
    DESTRUCTIVE resolution: the caller has independently confirmed (agent-tail,
    agent-msg, a live SendMessage reply, ...) that the bound agent is actually
    alive -- the orphan alert is a false positive, not a dead agent. Acking
    with this flag ALWAYS allows (bypasses the running-status lookup entirely)
    and does NOT touch the queue item -- no done/abandon/resurrect is called,
    so a live agent's q-id is never rotated out from under it (the da57->c740
    strand: resurrect rotated the q-id of a verified-alive agent and required
    an obligations-override to recover). The destructive resolutions
    (done/abandon/resurrect) remain available as a CHOICE for a genuinely dead
    agent; this flag is for the case they are the wrong choice.

    DEFAULT-OPEN: if the entry is not a queue-orphaned event, the q-id is
    unparseable, session-task is unavailable, or the lookup errors / times out /
    returns unparseable output, the ack is ALLOWED (and the reason logged to
    stderr). A verification failure must never blackhole the ack path.
    """
    source_event = (entry or {}).get("source_event", "") or ""
    if source_event not in QUEUE_ORPHANED_SOURCE_EVENTS:
        return (True, "")  # not a queue-orphaned event -- no gate

    if verified_false_positive:
        # Caller asserts they've confirmed liveness out-of-band. Allow
        # unconditionally -- no session-task lookup, no queue mutation.
        return (True, "")

    m = _QID_RE.search(key or "")
    if not m:
        print(f"event-ack: orphan-verify default-open: no q-id parseable "
              f"from key {key!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return (True, "")
    qid = m.group(0)

    cli = _resolve_session_task_cli()
    if not cli:
        print("event-ack: orphan-verify default-open: session-task "
              "unavailable", file=sys.stderr)
        return (True, "")

    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(
            [cli, "queue", "show", qid],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10, check=False,
        )
    except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as exc:
        print(f"event-ack: orphan-verify default-open: session-task show "
              f"failed for {qid}: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return (True, "")

    if proc.returncode != 0:
        print(f"event-ack: orphan-verify default-open: session-task show "
              f"{qid} exited {proc.returncode}", file=sys.stderr)
        return (True, "")

    try:
        status = json.loads(proc.stdout).get("status")
    except (ValueError, AttributeError) as exc:
        print(f"event-ack: orphan-verify default-open: could not parse "
              f"session-task show {qid}: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return (True, "")

    if status == "running":
        return (False,
                f"{qid} still running-orphaned -- resolve via "
                f"done/abandon/resurrect, OR if you have VERIFIED the agent "
                f"is actually alive (agent-tail / agent-msg / a live reply), "
                f"re-run with --verified-false-positive; ack alone does not "
                f"resolve it")
    return (True, "")


def list_state(state_dir: Path) -> dict:
    """Snapshot pending + counter for inspection."""
    pending = []
    with _locked(state_dir, PENDING_FILE) as p:
        pending = list(p["data"].get("pending", []))
    counter = _get_counter(state_dir)
    ambient_count = 0
    with _locked(state_dir, AMBIENT_FILE) as a:
        ambient_count = len(a["data"].get("events", []))
    return {"pending": pending, "counter": counter,
            "ambient_queued": ambient_count, "threshold": DEFAULT_N}


def clear_pending(state_dir: Path) -> dict:
    """Clear all pending entries. Reset counter."""
    n = 0
    with _locked(state_dir, PENDING_FILE) as p:
        n = len(p["data"].get("pending", []))
        p["data"]["pending"] = []
        p["write"] = True
    _set_counter(state_dir, 0)
    return {"cleared": n}


# --- N-counter ------------------------------------------------------------

def _get_counter(state_dir: Path) -> int:
    with _locked(state_dir, COUNTER_FILE) as c:
        v = c["data"].get("count", 0)
        return v if isinstance(v, int) and v >= 0 else 0


def _set_counter(state_dir: Path, value: int) -> None:
    with _locked(state_dir, COUNTER_FILE) as c:
        c["data"]["count"] = max(0, int(value))
        c["data"]["updated_at"] = _now()
        c["write"] = True


def bump_counter(state_dir: Path, by: int = 1) -> int:
    """Atomic increment. Returns the new value."""
    with _locked(state_dir, COUNTER_FILE) as c:
        cur = c["data"].get("count", 0)
        if not (isinstance(cur, int) and cur >= 0):
            cur = 0
        new = cur + by
        c["data"]["count"] = new
        c["data"]["updated_at"] = _now()
        c["write"] = True
        return new


def reset_counter(state_dir: Path) -> int:
    _set_counter(state_dir, 0)
    return 0


# --- Ambient queue --------------------------------------------------------

def queue_ambient(state_dir: Path, source: str, tag: str,
                  message: str, reason: str = "",
                  unclassified: bool = False) -> dict:
    """Append an ambient event to the inject queue. No counter touch."""
    with _locked(state_dir, AMBIENT_FILE) as a:
        events = a["data"].setdefault("events", [])
        entry = {
            "source": source, "tag": tag, "message": message,
            "reason": reason, "queued_at": _now(),
        }
        if unclassified:
            entry["unclassified"] = True
        events.append(entry)
        a["write"] = True
        return {"queued": True, "depth": len(events)}


def drain_ambient(state_dir: Path) -> list[dict]:
    """Pop and return all queued ambient events."""
    with _locked(state_dir, AMBIENT_FILE) as a:
        events = list(a["data"].get("events", []))
        a["data"]["events"] = []
        a["write"] = True
        return events


# --- Ingest (classify + route) --------------------------------------------

def _classify(source: str, tag: str, message: str,
              shipped_tier: str | None = None) -> dict:
    """Shell out to event-classify, with a Python-side fallback if the
    CLI is missing (tests / stripped containers). Both paths return
    {'tier': str, 'reason': str}. ``shipped_tier`` is the PRODUCER-shipped
    tier (from the event's ``data.tier``); when present it takes precedence
    over the consumer-side classifier table (see event-classify)."""
    cli = shutil.which("event-classify")
    if cli is None:
        # Sibling lookup (when running from source tree).
        here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
        sibling = here / "event-classify"
        if sibling.exists():
            cli = str(sibling)
    if cli is None:
        # Last-ditch: import the module in-process. Since event-classify
        # is a script (not a package), use exec on its source.
        return _classify_inline(source, tag, message, shipped_tier)
    try:
        cmd = [cli, "--source", source, "--tag", tag,
               "--message", message, "--json"]
        if shipped_tier:
            cmd += ["--tier", shipped_tier]
        proc = subprocess.run(
            cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5, check=False,
        )
        if proc.returncode == 0 and proc.stdout.strip():
            return json.loads(proc.stdout)
    except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError,
            json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):
        pass
    return _classify_inline(source, tag, message, shipped_tier)


def _classify_inline(source: str, tag: str, message: str,
                     shipped_tier: str | None = None) -> dict:
    """Fallback path: load event-classify's CLASSIFICATIONS table by
    exec'ing the file in a private namespace, then call classify()."""
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    sibling = here / "event-classify"
    if not sibling.exists():
        return {"tier": "ambient",
                "reason": "fallback: event-classify missing"}
    try:
        ns: dict = {"__name__": "__inline__"}
        exec(sibling.read_text(), ns)
        return ns["classify"](source, tag, message,
                              shipped_tier=shipped_tier)
    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001
        return {"tier": "ambient",
                "reason": f"fallback-error: {exc}"}


def ingest(state_dir: Path, source: str, tag: str,
           message: str, shipped_tier: str | None = None) -> dict:
    """Classify event and route to pending or ambient. Excluded
    events are no-op (Signal stays on its own gate). ``shipped_tier`` is the
    producer-shipped tier (event ``data.tier``); it takes precedence over the
    consumer-side table (see event-classify)."""
    cls = _classify(source, tag, message, shipped_tier)
    tier = cls.get("tier", "ambient")
    reason = cls.get("reason", "")
    unclassified = bool(cls.get("unclassified"))
    if tier == "excluded":
        return {"routed": "excluded", "tier": tier, "reason": reason,
                "unclassified": unclassified}
    if tier == "actionable":
        key = f"{tag}:{(message or '')[:80]}"
        add_pending(state_dir, key, source=f"{source}/{tag}",
                    reset_counter=True, reason=reason,
                    unclassified=unclassified)
        return {"routed": "pending", "tier": tier, "key": key,
                "reason": reason, "unclassified": unclassified}
    # ambient (or unknown -> defaults to ambient)
    queue_ambient(state_dir, source, tag, message, reason=reason,
                  unclassified=unclassified)
    return {"routed": "ambient", "tier": tier, "reason": reason,
            "unclassified": unclassified}


# --- CLI ------------------------------------------------------------------

def _build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="event-ack",
        description=__doc__,
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    p.add_argument("--state-dir", default=str(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR),
                   help=f"State directory (default: {DEFAULT_STATE_DIR}).")
    p.add_argument("--self-test", action="store_true",
                   help="Run the embedded test suite and exit.")

    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")

    sp = sub.add_parser("ingest", help="Classify + route an event.")
    sp.add_argument("--source", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--tag", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--message", default="")
    sp.add_argument("--tier", "--priority", dest="tier", default=None,
                    help="Producer-SHIPPED tier (actionable|ambient|excluded) "
                         "from the event's data.tier; takes precedence over "
                         "the consumer-side classifier table.")

    sp = sub.add_parser("add", help="Add a pending actionable entry.")
    sp.add_argument("key")
    sp.add_argument("--source", default="")

    sp = sub.add_parser("ack", help="Ack (remove) a pending entry.")
    sp.add_argument("key")
    sp.add_argument("--action", default=None,
                    help="what you did (one line). For text with backticks, "
                         "$(...) or $VARS use --action-file - with a QUOTED "
                         "heredoc instead: event-ack ack KEY --action-file - "
                         "<<'EOF' ... EOF")
    sp.add_argument("--action-file", default=None, metavar="FILE|-",
                    help="read the action text from FILE, or stdin with '-' "
                         "(exclusive with --action)")
    sp.add_argument(
        "--verified-false-positive", action="store_true",
        help="For a queue-orphaned key: the caller has independently "
             "confirmed the bound agent is actually alive (agent-tail / "
             "agent-msg / a live reply) -- clear the pending event without "
             "calling done/abandon/resurrect, so a live agent's q-id is "
             "never rotated out from under it. Only affects queue-orphaned "
             "keys; a no-op flag on any other key.")

    sp = sub.add_parser(
        "ack-batch",
        help="DISABLED (Andrew directive, 2026-09-11): always refuses, "
             "exits nonzero, touches NO state. Kept registered only so "
             "it stays discoverable here instead of erroring as unknown. "
             "Ack each pending event individually: `event-ack ack "
             "\"<key>\" --action \"...\"`.")
    sp.add_argument("--action", default="",
                    help="Accepted for backward compatibility; IGNORED.")
    sp.add_argument(
        "--override-reason", default="",
        help="Accepted for backward compatibility; IGNORED. ack-batch no "
             "longer accepts any override -- it is disabled unconditionally.")

    sub.add_parser("list", help="Show pending + counter state.")
    sub.add_parser("clear", help="Clear all pending entries.")
    sub.add_parser("drain-ambient",
                   help="(Hook-internal) Pop queued ambient events.")
    sub.add_parser("reset-counter", help="Reset N-counter to 0.")
    bp = sub.add_parser("bump-counter",
                        help="(Evaluator-internal) Increment N-counter.")
    bp.add_argument("--by", type=int, default=1)

    return p


_SUBCOMMANDS = frozenset({
    "ack", "ack-batch", "add", "ingest", "list", "clear",
    "drain-ambient", "reset-counter", "bump-counter",
})


def _legacy_dispatch(args: list[str]) -> int | None:
    """v1 compatibility: ``event-ack --add KEY`` / ``--list`` /
    ``--clear`` / ``<key> --action ...`` still work. Returns the
    exit code, or None if the args don't look legacy."""
    if not args:
        return None
    first = args[0]
    # If the first positional matches a real subcommand name, bail out
    # and let the argparse dispatcher handle it properly.
    if first in _SUBCOMMANDS:
        return None
    if first == "--add":
        if len(args) < 2:
            print("error: --add requires a key", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        key = args[1]
        source = ""
        i = 2
        while i < len(args):
            if args[i] == "--source" and i + 1 < len(args):
                source = args[i + 1]
                i += 2
            else:
                i += 1
        res = add_pending(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR, key, source=source)
        if res["added"]:
            print(f"Added: {key}")
        else:
            print(f"Already pending: {key}")
        return 0
    if first == "--list":
        snap = list_state(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR)
        if not snap["pending"]:
            print("No pending actionable events.")
        else:
            print(f"{len(snap['pending'])} pending actionable event(s):")
            for item in snap["pending"]:
                print(f"  - {item['key']}  (added: "
                      f"{item.get('added_at', '?')})")
        print(f"Tool-call counter: {snap['counter']} / "
              f"{snap['threshold']}")
        print(f"Ambient queued:    {snap['ambient_queued']}")
        return 0
    if first == "--clear":
        res = clear_pending(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR)
        print(f"Cleared {res['cleared']} pending event(s).")
        return 0
    # Legacy "event-ack <key> --action <text>" (positional + flag).
    if (not first.startswith("--") and len(args) >= 3
            and "--action" in args):
        key = first
        action = ""
        for i in range(1, len(args)):
            if args[i] == "--action" and i + 1 < len(args):
                action = args[i + 1]
                break
        if not action:
            print("error: --action requires a value", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        res = ack_pending(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR, key, action)
        if res["removed"]:
            print(f"Acked: {key} (action: {action})")
        else:
            print(f"Warning: \"{key}\" was not in pending list "
                  f"(already acked or never added)")
        if res["remaining"] > 0:
            print(f"{res['remaining']} event(s) still pending action.")
        else:
            print("All actionable events handled.")
        return 0
    return None


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    if argv is None:
        argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if argv and argv[0] == "--self-test":
        return _self_test()

    # v1 compat: handle bare --add / --list / --clear / "<key> --action".
    legacy = _legacy_dispatch(argv)
    if legacy is not None:
        return legacy

    parser = _build_parser()
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)

    if args.self_test:
        return _self_test()

    if args.cmd == "ingest":
        res = ingest(state_dir, args.source, args.tag, args.message,
                     shipped_tier=args.tier)
        print(json.dumps(res))
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "add":
        res = add_pending(state_dir, args.key, source=args.source)
        print(f"Added: {args.key}" if res["added"]
              else f"Already pending: {args.key}")
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "ack":
        if args.action is not None and args.action_file is not None:
            print("ERROR: --action and --action-file are mutually exclusive",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        if args.action is None and args.action_file is None:
            print("ERROR: give --action TEXT or --action-file FILE|-",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        if args.action_file is not None:
            try:
                if args.action_file == "-":
                    args.action = sys.stdin.read()
                else:
                    with open(args.action_file, "r") as _fh:
                        args.action = _fh.read()
            except OSError as e:
                print(f"ERROR: cannot read --action-file "
                      f"{args.action_file!r}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        action = (args.action or "").strip()
        entry = _find_pending_entry(state_dir, args.key)
        # Queue-orphaned events: an ack does NOT resolve the orphan. Refuse the
        # ack while the underlying queue item is still `running` -- it must be
        # resolved (done / abandon / resurrect) first, UNLESS the caller passes
        # --verified-false-positive to assert they've independently confirmed
        # the agent is alive (the escape hatch for the case the hard refusal
        # otherwise forces a destructive resurrect onto a live agent).
        # Default-open on any verification failure so a lookup problem never
        # blackholes the ack.
        ok, why = verify_orphan_resolved(
            entry, args.key,
            verified_false_positive=bool(args.verified_false_positive),
        )
        if not ok:
            print(f"REFUSED: {why}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        # A genuine actionable event REQUIRES a substantive --action: the ack
        # is the record of what you did. Pure-liveness entries (keepalive) and
        # idempotent no-ops (key not pending) do not.
        if entry is not None and not _is_liveness_entry(entry) and not action:
            print(
                "ERROR: --action must be non-empty when acking an actionable "
                f"event. Say what you did, e.g. event-ack ack \"{args.key}\" "
                "--action \"queued agent to handle it\".",
                file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        res = ack_pending(state_dir, args.key, args.action)
        if res["removed"]:
            print(f"Acked: {args.key} (action: {args.action})")
        else:
            print(f"Warning: \"{args.key}\" was not pending "
                  f"(idempotent no-op)")
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "ack-batch":
        # PERMANENTLY DISABLED (Andrew directive, 2026-09-11,
        # #7784/7786/7787): this subcommand became a reflexive per-event
        # bypass instead of a deliberate escape hatch. It now does
        # NOTHING -- no pending removal, no counter reset, no liveness
        # stamp -- regardless of what flags are passed (a real
        # --override-reason changes nothing: there is no override any
        # more). Ack every pending event individually instead.
        snap = list_state(state_dir)
        pending_keys = [e.get("key", "?") for e in snap.get("pending", [])]
        print(
            "ERROR: `event-ack ack-batch` is PERMANENTLY DISABLED. It "
            "performed NO action: no pending entry was removed, the "
            "N-counter was not reset, and the liveness timestamp was NOT "
            "stamped. Ack every pending event individually instead:\n"
            "  event-ack list\n"
            "  event-ack ack \"<key>\" --action \"<what you did>\"",
            file=sys.stderr)
        if pending_keys:
            print(f"{len(pending_keys)} pending key(s) still need a "
                  "per-event ack:", file=sys.stderr)
            for k in pending_keys:
                print(f"  event-ack ack \"{k}\" --action \"<what you did>\"",
                      file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    if args.cmd == "list":
        snap = list_state(state_dir)
        print(json.dumps(snap, indent=2))
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "clear":
        res = clear_pending(state_dir)
        print(f"Cleared {res['cleared']} pending event(s).")
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "drain-ambient":
        events = drain_ambient(state_dir)
        if not events:
            return 0
        # Emit a compact context block for the user-prompt hook to
        # surface. Plain text is fine -- Claude Code injects it
        # verbatim into the next prompt's context.
        lines = ["[AMBIENT EVENTS — informational context, no action "
                 "required unless something stands out]"]
        for e in events:
            src = e.get("source", "?")
            tg = e.get("tag", "?")
            msg = (e.get("message") or "").strip()
            if msg:
                lines.append(f"  - [{src}/{tg}] {msg}")
            else:
                lines.append(f"  - [{src}/{tg}]")
        print("\n".join(lines))
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "reset-counter":
        reset_counter(state_dir)
        print("Counter reset to 0.")
        return 0

    if args.cmd == "bump-counter":
        new = bump_counter(state_dir, by=args.by)
        print(str(new))
        return 0

    parser.print_help()
    return 1


# --- Embedded self-test ---------------------------------------------------

def _self_test() -> int:
    import tempfile
    failures: list[str] = []

    # Pin classification to OUR sibling event-classify. `_classify` prefers
    # `shutil.which("event-classify")`, which in a dev checkout resolves to
    # the INSTALLED copy on PATH -- so without this the suite would validate
    # whatever is deployed on the host rather than the code in this tree, and
    # a green run would prove nothing about the change under test.
    os.environ["PATH"] = (str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent)
                          + os.pathsep + os.environ.get("PATH", ""))
    # Also isolate from a real operator override file (rung 1 of the
    # precedence ladder) so host config can't flip an expected tier.
    os.environ["EVENT_CLASSIFY_OVERRIDES"] = str(
        Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / "event-ack-self-test-no-such-file")

    def fail(msg: str) -> None:
        failures.append(msg)

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:
        sd = Path(td)

        # 1. List on empty state: no pending, counter=0, ambient=0.
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["pending"] or snap["counter"] != 0 or snap["ambient_queued"] != 0:
            fail(f"empty state: {snap}")

        # 2. Add pending -> appears in list.
        add_pending(sd, "torrent-completed:foo")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if len(snap["pending"]) != 1 or snap["counter"] != 0:
            fail(f"after add: {snap}")

        # 3. Idempotent add (same key).
        add_pending(sd, "torrent-completed:foo")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if len(snap["pending"]) != 1:
            fail(f"idempotent add duplicated: {snap}")

        # 4. Bump counter while pending.
        n1 = bump_counter(sd)
        n2 = bump_counter(sd)
        if (n1, n2) != (1, 2):
            fail(f"counter bump: got ({n1}, {n2}) expected (1, 2)")

        # 5. Ack resets counter.
        ack_pending(sd, "torrent-completed:foo", "queued agent")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["pending"] or snap["counter"] != 0:
            fail(f"after ack: {snap}")

        # 6. Ack of non-existent key is idempotent (no error).
        res = ack_pending(sd, "nonexistent", "test")
        if res["removed"]:
            fail(f"non-existent ack should not flip removed=True: {res}")

        # 7. Adding a SECOND pending key while counter is high resets to 0
        #    (each event gets a fresh grace window).
        add_pending(sd, "k1")
        bump_counter(sd, by=2)  # counter -> 2
        add_pending(sd, "k2")  # should reset
        if _get_counter(sd) != 0:
            fail(f"add should reset counter; got {_get_counter(sd)}")
        clear_pending(sd)

        # 8. Clear removes everything + resets counter.
        add_pending(sd, "a")
        add_pending(sd, "b")
        bump_counter(sd, by=5)
        res = clear_pending(sd)
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if res["cleared"] != 2 or snap["pending"] or snap["counter"] != 0:
            fail(f"clear: {res} / {snap}")

        # 9. Ingest routes ambient correctly.
        ingest(sd, "alertmanager", "alert-firing", "FooAlert firing")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["ambient_queued"] != 1 or snap["pending"]:
            fail(f"ambient ingest: {snap}")

        # 10. Ingest routes actionable correctly.
        ingest(sd, "torrent", "torrent-completed", "Movie X done")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if not snap["pending"] or len(snap["pending"]) != 1:
            fail(f"actionable ingest: {snap}")

        # 11. Ingest routes excluded (signal) to nothing.
        ingest(sd, "manual", "signal-dm-inbound", "from alice")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        # pending count still 1 (the prior torrent), ambient still 1.
        if len(snap["pending"]) != 1 or snap["ambient_queued"] != 1:
            fail(f"signal exclusion leaked: {snap}")

        # 11b. Producer-SHIPPED tier routes actionable even when the message
        # alone would classify ambient (botchat #3879: the producer stamps
        # data.tier=actionable on its unresolved-comment events). Routed by the
        # shipped tier, NOT a message regex.
        clear_pending(sd)
        ingest(sd, "cron", "pr-status-change",
               "PR foo/bar#12: 3 unresolved comment(s) (was: 0)",
               shipped_tier="actionable")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if len(snap["pending"]) != 1:
            fail(f"shipped-tier actionable ingest: {snap}")
        # Same event with NO shipped tier -> ambient (consumer catch-all).
        ambient_before = snap["ambient_queued"]
        ingest(sd, "cron", "pr-status-change",
               "PR foo/bar#12: 4 unresolved comment(s) (was: 3)")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["ambient_queued"] != ambient_before + 1:
            fail(f"unstamped unresolved-comment should be ambient: {snap}")

        # 11c. UNCLASSIFIED propagation (botchat #2483). A pair with no rule
        # and no producer-shipped tier still routes actionable (fail-loud,
        # unchanged) but the entry is MARKED and carries the directive
        # reason, so the gate can render "add a rule" instead of a mystery.
        clear_pending(sd)
        res = ingest(sd, "novel-source", "novel-tag", "something new")
        if res["routed"] != "pending" or not res.get("unclassified"):
            fail(f"unclassified ingest: {res}")
        entry = list_state(sd)["pending"][0]
        if not entry.get("unclassified"):
            fail(f"unclassified flag not persisted on entry: {entry}")
        if "data.tier" not in entry.get("reason", ""):
            fail(f"directive reason not persisted: {entry}")

        # A CLASSIFIED actionable event must NOT be marked (no false noise).
        clear_pending(sd)
        res = ingest(sd, "torrent", "torrent-completed", "done")
        if res["routed"] != "pending" or res.get("unclassified"):
            fail(f"classified event wrongly marked unclassified: {res}")
        if list_state(sd)["pending"][0].get("unclassified"):
            fail("classified entry carries an unclassified flag")

        # 11d. pr-status-change: "CI success" is AMBIENT now (#2484/#2485),
        # "CI failure" stays ACTIONABLE on the transition itself -- so a
        # newly-red PR is actionable immediately, with no ambient window
        # before the separate pr-ci-red nudge.
        clear_pending(sd)
        if ingest(sd, "cron", "pr-status-change",
                  "PR o/r#642: CI success (was: pending)")["tier"] != "ambient":
            fail("CI success should be ambient")
        if ingest(sd, "cron", "pr-status-change",
                  "PR o/r#642: CI failure (was: pending)")["tier"] \
                != "actionable":
            fail("CI failure must stay actionable")

        # 12. Drain ambient -> empties queue + returns events.
        events = drain_ambient(sd)
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if not events or snap["ambient_queued"] != 0:
            fail(f"drain ambient: events={len(events)} snap={snap}")

        # 13. Reset counter directly.
        bump_counter(sd, by=3)
        reset_counter(sd)
        if _get_counter(sd) != 0:
            fail(f"reset_counter didn't zero: {_get_counter(sd)}")

        # 14. Corrupt state file -> default-open (treated as empty).
        clear_pending(sd)
        (sd / PENDING_FILE).write_text("{not valid json")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["pending"]:
            fail(f"corrupt state should be empty: {snap}")

        # 15. Concurrent add+ack stress: 50 add+ack cycles in sequence
        #     under the lock should never lose a row.
        for i in range(50):
            add_pending(sd, f"stress-{i}")
            ack_pending(sd, f"stress-{i}", "test")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if snap["pending"] or snap["counter"] != 0:
            fail(f"stress cycle leaked state: {snap}")

        # 16. Concurrent processes hold the lock (real fork test).
        # Two child processes that both increment counter 20 times each
        # should land at exactly 40, never less, regardless of interleave.
        reset_counter(sd)
        pids = []
        for _ in range(2):
            pid = os.fork()
            if pid == 0:
                # child
                for _ in range(20):
                    bump_counter(sd)
                os._exit(0)
            pids.append(pid)
        for pid in pids:
            os.waitpid(pid, 0)
        final = _get_counter(sd)
        if final != 40:
            fail(f"concurrent bump: expected 40, got {final}")

        # 17. Legacy dispatch does NOT intercept subcommand names.
        #     "event-ack ack <key> --action <text>" must return None from
        #     _legacy_dispatch so argparse handles it.
        add_pending(sd, "sub-test-key")
        legacy_result = _legacy_dispatch(
            ["ack", "sub-test-key", "--action", "via argparse"])
        if legacy_result is not None:
            fail(f"_legacy_dispatch intercepted 'ack' subcommand: "
                 f"returned {legacy_result}")
        # Verify argparse path works (via main()).
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", "sub-test-key",
                   "--action", "via argparse"])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"argparse ack returned rc={rc}")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if any(e["key"] == "sub-test-key" for e in snap["pending"]):
            fail(f"sub-test-key still pending after argparse ack: {snap}")

        # 18. ack-batch is PERMANENTLY DISABLED (Andrew directive,
        #     2026-09-11, #7784/7786/7787): a bare invocation with pending
        #     liveness + actionable entries must hard-refuse (nonzero exit)
        #     and touch NOTHING -- no pending removed, no counter reset, no
        #     liveness stamp. The old "clear only liveness entries" carve-out
        #     is gone: nothing is cleared any more, full stop.
        clear_pending(sd)
        ingest(sd, "claude-watch", "keepalive", "idle poke")         # liveness
        ingest(sd, "claude-watch", "heartbeat-tick", "legacy poke")  # liveness
        ingest(sd, "torrent", "torrent-completed", "Movie done")     # actionable
        add_pending(sd, "slack-unread:from bob")                     # actionable
        bump_counter(sd)
        stamp = sd / LAST_ACK_FILE
        if stamp.exists():
            stamp.unlink()
        before = list_state(sd)
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack-batch"])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("bare `event-ack ack-batch` must hard-refuse (nonzero exit)")
        after = list_state(sd)
        if after != before:
            fail(f"ack-batch must not mutate pending/counter state: "
                 f"before={before} after={after}")
        if stamp.exists():
            fail("disabled ack-batch must NOT write last-ack-timestamp")

        # 19. Flags (--action, --override-reason) are accepted for backward
        #     compatibility but change NOTHING: still refuses, still no
        #     state mutation, regardless of what's passed.
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack-batch", "--action", "x",
                   "--override-reason", "reviewed everything"])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("ack-batch with flags must still hard-refuse")
        after2 = list_state(sd)
        if after2 != before:
            fail(f"ack-batch with flags must not mutate state: {after2}")
        if stamp.exists():
            fail("ack-batch with flags must NOT write last-ack-timestamp")

        # 20. ack-batch on an EMPTY queue also refuses -- there is no more
        #     "idle loop proving it's alive via batch-ack" path. Liveness
        #     now comes ONLY from per-key ack (see #21).
        clear_pending(sd)
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack-batch"])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("ack-batch on an empty queue must still hard-refuse")
        if stamp.exists():
            fail("ack-batch on an empty queue must NOT stamp liveness")

        # 21. Liveness now comes ONLY from per-key `ack` -- including for a
        #     pure-liveness (keepalive) entry, which has no substantive
        #     --action note but still stamps last-ack-timestamp.
        clear_pending(sd)
        ingest(sd, "claude-watch", "keepalive", "solo poke")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        keepalive_key = next(e["key"] for e in snap["pending"])
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", keepalive_key,
                   "--action", "keepalive"])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"per-key ack of a keepalive entry returned rc={rc}")
        if list_state(sd)["pending"]:
            fail("per-key ack of the only pending entry must clear it")
        if not stamp.exists():
            fail("per-key ack must write last-ack-timestamp")
        else:
            try:
                stamped = float(stamp.read_text().strip())
            except ValueError:
                stamped = -1.0
                fail(f"last-ack-timestamp must be a parseable epoch, got "
                     f"{stamp.read_text()!r}")
            now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).timestamp()
            if not (0 < now - stamped < 60):
                fail(f"last-ack stamp {stamped} should be ~now ({now})")

        # 22. Legacy dispatch must not swallow the (disabled) subcommand name.
        if _legacy_dispatch(["ack-batch"]) is not None:
            fail("_legacy_dispatch intercepted the 'ack-batch' subcommand")

        # 23. Per-key ack of an ACTIONABLE event REQUIRES a non-empty --action
        #     (the ack IS the record of what you did); the counter resets on a
        #     real per-key actionable ack.
        clear_pending(sd)
        ingest(sd, "torrent", "torrent-completed", "Movie Y done")
        akey = list_state(sd)["pending"][0]["key"]
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", akey, "--action", "   "])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("per-key ack of an actionable event with blank --action "
                 "must be refused")
        if not any(e["key"] == akey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("refused per-key ack must not remove the actionable entry")
        bump_counter(sd, by=2)
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", akey,
                   "--action", "queued download agent"])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"per-key ack with a real --action returned rc={rc}")
        snap = list_state(sd)
        if any(e["key"] == akey for e in snap["pending"]) or snap["counter"] != 0:
            fail(f"per-key actionable ack must remove entry + reset counter: {snap}")

        # 24. Per-key ack of a pure-liveness entry does NOT require a
        #     substantive --action (nothing to do beyond proving liveness).
        clear_pending(sd)
        ingest(sd, "claude-watch", "keepalive", "poke2")
        lkey = list_state(sd)["pending"][0]["key"]
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", lkey, "--action", ""])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"per-key ack of a liveness entry with empty --action should "
                 f"be allowed, got rc={rc}")
        if any(e["key"] == lkey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("per-key liveness ack must remove the entry")

        # ---- Orphan-ack verification (queue-orphaned events) --------------
        # A queue-orphaned event marks a `running` queue item with no live
        # owner; acking it does NOT resolve the orphan. verify_orphan_resolved
        # refuses the ack while the item is still `running`, and default-opens
        # on any lookup problem. A fake `session-task` on PATH returns a
        # controllable status so the whole gate is exercised without a live
        # queue. It takes precedence over the real sibling CLI (which
        # `_resolve_session_task_cli` only falls back to when PATH has none).
        fake_bin = sd / "fakebin"
        fake_bin.mkdir()
        fake_st = fake_bin / "session-task"
        fake_st.write_text(
            "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
            "printf '{\"status\": \"%s\"}\\n' \"${FAKE_ST_STATUS:-running}\"\n"
            "exit \"${FAKE_ST_RC:-0}\"\n"
        )
        fake_st.chmod(0o755)
        os.environ["PATH"] = str(fake_bin) + os.pathsep + os.environ["PATH"]

        orphan_entry = {"source_event": "queue/queue-orphaned"}
        cw_orphan_entry = {"source_event": "claude-watch/queue-orphaned"}
        orphan_key = "queue-orphaned:q-2026-01-02-abcd running w/o owner"

        # 25. Non-orphan source_event -> always allowed (no lookup gate).
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(
            {"source_event": "torrent/torrent-completed"}, "k:x")
        if not ok:
            fail("non-orphan entry must be allowed by verify_orphan_resolved")
        # None entry (idempotent no-op ack of an absent key) -> allowed.
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(None, orphan_key)
        if not ok:
            fail("None entry must be allowed by verify_orphan_resolved")

        # 26. Orphan + status running -> REFUSED, for BOTH source spellings.
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "running"
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_RC"] = "0"
        ok, msg = verify_orphan_resolved(orphan_entry, orphan_key)
        if ok or "still running-orphaned" not in msg or \
                "q-2026-01-02-abcd" not in msg:
            fail(f"running orphan must be refused: ok={ok} msg={msg!r}")
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(cw_orphan_entry, orphan_key)
        if ok:
            fail("running orphan (claude-watch source) must be refused")

        # 27. Orphan + a non-running status -> ALLOWED.
        for st_val in ("done", "abandoned", "blocked", "pending"):
            os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = st_val
            ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(orphan_entry, orphan_key)
            if not ok:
                fail(f"orphan with status {st_val} must be allowed")

        # 28. Orphan but q-id unparseable -> DEFAULT-OPEN (allow).
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "running"
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(orphan_entry, "queue-orphaned:no id here")
        if not ok:
            fail("unparseable q-id must default-open (allow)")

        # 29. Orphan + session-task exits non-zero -> DEFAULT-OPEN (allow).
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_RC"] = "1"
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(orphan_entry, orphan_key)
        if not ok:
            fail("session-task non-zero exit must default-open (allow)")
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_RC"] = "0"

        # 30. End-to-end via main(): a running-orphan ack is REFUSED (rc!=0)
        #     and the pending entry is NOT removed.
        clear_pending(sd)
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "running"
        ingest(sd, "queue", "queue-orphaned",
               "q-2026-01-02-abcd running without owner")
        okey = list_state(sd)["pending"][0]["key"]
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", okey,
                   "--action", "looked at it"])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("main() ack of a running-orphan must be refused")
        if not any(e["key"] == okey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("refused running-orphan ack must not remove the entry")

        # 31. End-to-end via main(): once resolved (done), the ack SUCCEEDS.
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "done"
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", okey,
                   "--action", "resurrected then marked done"])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"main() ack of a resolved orphan must succeed, got rc={rc}")
        if any(e["key"] == okey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("resolved-orphan ack must remove the entry")

        # ---- --verified-false-positive escape hatch (q-0151 / da57->c740) -
        # A running-orphan ack normally forces done/abandon/resurrect, which
        # for a demonstrably LIVE agent means a destructive queue mutation
        # (resurrect rotates the q-id, stranding the live agent -- the
        # da57->c740 incident, recovered only via an obligations-override).
        # --verified-false-positive asserts the caller independently
        # confirmed liveness and clears the pending event WITHOUT touching
        # the queue item at all.

        # 32. verify_orphan_resolved(verified_false_positive=True) bypasses
        #     the running check entirely -- allowed even with status=running
        #     and even if session-task is made to error.
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "running"
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_RC"] = "0"
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(
            orphan_entry, orphan_key, verified_false_positive=True)
        if not ok:
            fail("verified_false_positive=True must bypass a running orphan")
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(
            cw_orphan_entry, orphan_key, verified_false_positive=True)
        if not ok:
            fail("verified_false_positive=True must bypass (claude-watch source)")

        # 33. The flag is a harmless no-op on a NON-orphan entry (nothing to
        #     bypass -- still just allowed, as it always was).
        ok, _m = verify_orphan_resolved(
            {"source_event": "torrent/torrent-completed"}, "k:x",
            verified_false_positive=True)
        if not ok:
            fail("verified_false_positive=True must be a no-op on non-orphan")

        # 34. End-to-end via main(): `ack --verified-false-positive` clears a
        #     running-orphan pending entry WITHOUT ever calling session-task
        #     (status stays "running" throughout -- if the CLI mutated the
        #     queue, a bug would have to actively avoid doing so to pass;
        #     the real assertion is that the ack SUCCEEDS and the entry is
        #     gone despite status=running never changing).
        clear_pending(sd)
        os.environ["FAKE_ST_STATUS"] = "running"
        ingest(sd, "queue", "queue-orphaned",
               "q-2026-01-02-face running without owner")
        fkey = list_state(sd)["pending"][0]["key"]
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", fkey,
                   "--action", "confirmed alive via agent-tail",
                   "--verified-false-positive"])
        if rc != 0:
            fail(f"main() ack --verified-false-positive must succeed, got rc={rc}")
        if any(e["key"] == fkey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("verified-false-positive ack must remove the entry")
        if os.environ.get("FAKE_ST_STATUS") != "running":
            fail("verified-false-positive ack must not have mutated session-task state")

        # 35. Without --action, --verified-false-positive still requires the
        #     substantive-action rule (the ack is the record of WHAT was
        #     verified) -- rejected before verify_orphan_resolved is reached.
        ingest(sd, "queue", "queue-orphaned",
               "q-2026-01-02-cafe running without owner")
        gkey = next(e["key"] for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]
                    if e["key"] != fkey)
        rc = main(["--state-dir", str(sd), "ack", gkey,
                   "--action", "", "--verified-false-positive"])
        if rc == 0:
            fail("verified-false-positive ack with empty --action must still "
                 "be rejected")
        if not any(e["key"] == gkey for e in list_state(sd)["pending"]):
            fail("rejected empty-action ack must not remove the entry")

        for _k in ("FAKE_ST_STATUS", "FAKE_ST_RC"):
            os.environ.pop(_k, None)

    if failures:
        print(f"FAIL: {len(failures)} case(s):", file=sys.stderr)
        for f in failures:
            print(f"  {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print("OK: all self-test cases pass (incl. ack-batch PERMANENTLY "
          "DISABLED -- hard-refuses and touches no state under any flags "
          "or queue contents -- per-key ack is now the only liveness path, "
          "per-key actionable ack requires --action, gate/counter resets).")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        sys.exit(130)
    except BrokenPipeError:
        # Common in shell pipelines (e.g. `event-ack list | head`).
        sys.exit(0)
